<deck title="ah-r animation" />

# Animation

Frame-by-frame `<animation>` — a flipbook of literal `<frame>`s, advancing
every `seconds`, optionally `loop`ing.

---

## A looping spinner

<animation seconds="0.12" loop>
<frame>
   |
</frame>
<frame>
   /
</frame>
<frame>
   -
</frame>
<frame>
   \
</frame>
</animation>

`seconds="0.12" loop` — spins in place forever.

---

## Same width, blinks in place

<animation seconds="0.4" loop>
<frame>
 /\_/\
( o.o )
 > ^ <
</frame>
<frame>
 /\_/\
( -.- )
 > ^ <
</frame>
</animation>

---

## Plays once, holds the last frame

<animation seconds="0.7">
<frame>
3
</frame>
<frame>
2
</frame>
<frame>
1
</frame>
<frame>
go!
</frame>
</animation>

No `loop` — it counts down once and stays on `go!`.

---

